# Visual Fidelity

**Applies to**: All UI implementation work

## Before Writing UI Code

Read these design artefacts:

1. `{project-root}/artefacts/design/design-system.md` (foundations §1, components §3 and §8, wireframes §7)
2. `visual-standards.md` for hierarchy, spacing, responsive rules

## Creative Latitude

Wireframes are a starting point, not a pixel-perfect spec. Agents may improve on wireframes — better layouts, clearer hierarchy, improved interactions are encouraged. But the design intent (information hierarchy, user flow, component choices) must be preserved. Document deviations in the handoff with rationale.

## During Implementation

- Use design tokens (not hardcoded values)
- Implement all states: empty, loading, error, populated
- Test at breakpoints from visual-standards.md
- If improving on the wireframe, document what changed and why in handoff

## Forbidden

- Building UI without reading design artefacts first
- Skipping empty/loading/error states
- Ignoring responsive breakpoints
- Deviating from wireframe without documenting rationale
